Pin CUDA modular-beam forward and backprojection to their Joseph branches.

Target: LLNL/LEAP version 1.26, upstream commit 0c8846f42b2e59340d5559fc1271d590a292f9a0.
https://github.com/LLNL/LEAP
Extends the forward-only patch from Flow_matching_motion_3D commit
927eaacb785b98a3b742144d46c248c758302fb6 to also disable the SF/eSF
backprojection branches. The default remains false.
This pins kernel selection; it does not guarantee exact adjointness.
The get_forceJosephModularBackprojection C/Python getter checks capability
and enabled state, so an older forward-only shared library fails explicitly.

Apply from the upstream LEAP root:
    git apply --check /path/to/leap_force_joseph.patch
    git apply /path/to/leap_force_joseph.patch
Rebuild the shared library and use the matching patched src/leapctype.py.
    cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build --parallel 8
Using PYTHONPATH=/path/to/LEAP/src lets leapctype find ../build/lib/libleapct.so.

